  "_why": [
    "One file per CATEGORY, not per bucket, so a reviewer can see the whole",
    "argument for one category in one place and so a category can be re-run alone",
    "(--category matches these files' categories). boundary_d10.jsonl is the ONE",
    "exception: it collects the four open decision items D10 across two categories,",
    "because a boundary RULING is reviewed as a set rather than per category.",
    "",
    "This manifest is the version stamp the report records. Changing a case file",
    "without changing dataset_version makes two reports incomparable, which is the",
    "one thing an eval must not allow - so --dry-run fails when the manifest's",
    "counts disagree with the files."
